1
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:11,120
Dad.

2
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:14,200
Please take care of Grandma for me.

3
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:15,320
PREVIOUSLY

4
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:19,440
Whatever happens, you have
to accept it and fight through it.

5
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:22,760
I'll allow you to stay in this house.

6
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:24,920
But only because you are Hathaya's mother.

7
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,760
I only need to use it once

8
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:30,520
to get them thrown out of this house.

9
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:33,560
What are you doing?

10
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:48,600
What was that?

11
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:52,080
Did Chayanee say something that upset you?

12
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:54,720
She's jealous of me.

13
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:57,760
She thinks I'm stealing Raiwin.

14
00:03:59,880 --> 00:04:01,000
And…

15
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:05,360
Are you?

16
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:12,200
Then if you're not,
there's nothing to worry about.

17
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:15,080
I still feel bad about it.

18
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:17,600
You can't care what everyone thinks.

19
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:22,040
If you carry everyone's
feelings around with you,

20
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:25,240
when are you ever going to be happy?

21
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:31,560
If you're going to care about someone…

22
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:36,640
you could care about the people

23
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:39,000
close to you.

24
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:46,080
You're right.

25
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:50,040
I should pay more attention
to Grandpa and Mom.

26
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:56,520
Right.

27
00:04:57,480 --> 00:05:01,480
Although I think there might be

28
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:05,840
another good person close to you

29
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:08,400
who deserves some attention too.

30
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:13,800
Thank you so much.

31
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:17,040
I'll pay more attention
to the workers too.

32
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,440
You really didn't think of me?

33
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:54,640
Why did you call me?

34
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:00,200
What was that for?

35
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:05,120
-Chayanee.
-Don't raise your voice at me.

36
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:10,320
I'm knocking some sense into you.
If I call for you,

37
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:12,000
you come to me immediately.

38
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:14,400
Don't make me call you twice.
You're embarrassing me.

39
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:16,480
And you think I'm not embarrassed?

40
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:19,280
You shouted my name
like I was your servant.

41
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:21,280
You're not my servant.

42
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:24,680
But you belong to me. Not Hathaya.

43
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:26,800
What does she have to do with this?

44
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:29,320
I'm not blind.

45
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:32,760
I saw you deliberately holding her hand.

46
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:36,040
If I'd shown up a little later,
you'd have dragged her off somewhere.

47
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:39,320
We were only talking.

48
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:42,800
I was asking her to help campaign for me.

49
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:46,440
You already have me. I can do that job.

50
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:48,920
You don't need that parasite.

51
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:53,840
From now on, wherever you go
and whatever you do, you tell me.

52
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:55,440
Stay where I can keep an eye on you.

53
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:03,840
Am I your boyfriend or your prisoner?

54
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:18,200
If you were my prisoner,

55
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:24,160
I wouldn't even let you question me.

56
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:30,000
Don't forget what you promised me.

57
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:33,200
You said you wouldn't hurt me again.

58
00:07:38,320 --> 00:07:39,880
I'm going to touch up my makeup.

59
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:42,360
You're coming to the shrine with me.

60
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:54,000
Ramil.

61
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:07,320
Ramil, you don't deserve this.

62
00:08:15,240 --> 00:08:17,880
Madam. Madam. Madam.

63
00:08:17,960 --> 00:08:20,000
"Madam, Madam, Madam."

64
00:08:20,080 --> 00:08:23,040
Madam, let me speak first.

65
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:26,200
You yell for me all day long.
What is it now?

66
00:08:26,280 --> 00:08:29,200
It's your rival.

67
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:31,720
She's putting on a show,
acting like some heroine

68
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:33,919
in the middle of a lavender field.

69
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,159
A lavender field?

70
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:38,679
Wait. Since when
do we have a lavender field here?

71
00:08:38,760 --> 00:08:42,039
Oh, come on, madam.
It's a figure of speech.

72
00:08:42,559 --> 00:08:44,680
She's in the rose garden,

73
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:47,360
acting like the star of some drama.

74
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:50,720
-Really?
-Yes. I'll show you. Come on.

75
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:56,200
Alright.

76
00:08:58,920 --> 00:08:59,960
Pong.

77
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:03,040
Pong.

78
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:06,920
Madam, I think he might be asleep.

79
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:12,160
I'll step up and wake him.

80
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:13,600
Absolutely not.

81
00:09:13,680 --> 00:09:15,120
Go find something else to do. Go.

82
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:17,600
I'm free today. I have nothing to do.

83
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:24,040
I just remembered.

84
00:09:24,120 --> 00:09:26,640
I haven't cleaned the bedrooms yet.
I should go do that.

85
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:28,080
-Go.
-Yes, madam.

86
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:31,080
-Okay…
-Hurry.

87
00:09:40,600 --> 00:09:41,800
So possessive.

88
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:48,200
Why are you still here?

89
00:09:48,280 --> 00:09:49,440
I'm going.

90
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:55,200
Pong.

91
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:00,360
Pong.

92
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:14,200
Pong!

93
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:15,160
It's me.

94
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:19,720
Sorry.

95
00:10:20,640 --> 00:10:24,360
I thought someone dangerous had broken in.

96
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:29,440
Why don't you put some clothes on?

97
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:32,000
I have an urgent job for you.

98
00:10:37,040 --> 00:10:38,800
If it's that urgent,

99
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:41,520
just tell me now. I'm listening.

100
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:46,600
I want you to get close to Hathai,

101
00:10:46,680 --> 00:10:48,200
Hathaya's mother,

102
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:51,520
and lure her into your trap.

103
00:10:52,440 --> 00:10:53,880
You picked the right man for it.

104
00:10:57,800 --> 00:11:00,360
Don't mess this up
like you did at the construction site.

105
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:03,600
Otherwise, I won't keep you around.

106
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:05,840
I won't mess up again.

107
00:11:08,360 --> 00:11:10,600
You know I'm good at getting close

108
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:14,680
to women.

109
00:11:30,680 --> 00:11:31,600
Hey.

110
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:35,600
It's your day off. You came
all the way here to see me.

111
00:11:35,680 --> 00:11:37,080
Is something wrong?

112
00:11:37,640 --> 00:11:39,680
You could've just called.

113
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:41,520
I wanted to see you.

114
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:50,440
I mean there's something important
I need to discuss with you in person.

115
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:52,480
Oh.

116
00:11:53,960 --> 00:11:55,040
What is it?

117
00:11:56,320 --> 00:11:59,600
Ask Hathaya to help campaign for me.

118
00:11:59,680 --> 00:12:02,480
I think you should ask Hathaya yourself.

119
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:04,800
But she listens to you.

120
00:12:05,480 --> 00:12:09,720
Help me this once. Consider it repayment
for the favor I did for you.

121
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:12,760
Raiwin asked me to talk to you.

122
00:12:14,120 --> 00:12:15,360
He wants your help campaigning.

123
00:12:18,640 --> 00:12:21,440
And what do you think?

124
00:12:22,040 --> 00:12:23,040
Hm.

125
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:26,160
I want you

126
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:28,800
to help him.

127
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:33,720
Why do you want to help him

128
00:12:33,800 --> 00:12:35,920
after the way he's treated you?

129
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:38,800
Raiwin may seem selfish.

130
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:41,160
But a lot of that

131
00:12:41,840 --> 00:12:43,560
comes from how his father controlled him.

132
00:12:45,440 --> 00:12:48,600
I think Raiwin wants
a chance to be himself too.

133
00:12:48,680 --> 00:12:50,560
And up until now,

134
00:12:50,640 --> 00:12:52,800
he's never really accomplished
anything on his own.

135
00:12:54,160 --> 00:12:55,400
And there's something else.

136
00:12:55,480 --> 00:12:57,960
If Papang ever learns

137
00:12:58,840 --> 00:13:00,960
that Raiwin is his real father,

138
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:04,000
I want him to be proud of Raiwin.

139
00:13:12,280 --> 00:13:15,360
I'm ready, sweetheart. Shall we go?

140
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:19,240
Mom. I need to go take care
of something with Ramil.

141
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:24,440
Can you wait until I get back?
Then I'll take you shopping.

142
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:29,080
It's okay. Don't worry about me.

143
00:13:29,160 --> 00:13:31,440
I used to live here. I can go by myself.

144
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:35,960
Then at least let Aunt Ann
go with you. I worry about you.

145
00:13:37,800 --> 00:13:38,680
Alright.

146
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:42,240
Take care of my daughter for me.

147
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:46,280
I will.

148
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:50,360
I'm going now, Mom.

149
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:51,880
Take care.

150
00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:05,560
Ann?

151
00:14:06,680 --> 00:14:07,600
Ann?

152
00:14:08,320 --> 00:14:10,040
Ann isn't here.

153
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:12,720
Father wanted chive dumplings
from down the street.

154
00:14:13,840 --> 00:14:14,760
What do you want?

155
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:17,800
I'm going out. I was going to ask
Ann to come with me.

156
00:14:19,680 --> 00:14:22,160
I'm free. Want me to go with you?

157
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:27,240
I'm free too. I'd be happy
to look after you, Ms. Hathai.

158
00:14:27,320 --> 00:14:28,720
Thank you,

159
00:14:29,560 --> 00:14:32,040
but there's no need. I can go by myself.

160
00:14:33,720 --> 00:14:37,400
There are all kinds of scammers
out there these days.

161
00:14:38,080 --> 00:14:39,400
Be careful.

162
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:56,560
Madam, what did you plan with Pong?

163
00:14:58,560 --> 00:14:59,400
You want to know?

164
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:00,680
Yes.

165
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:05,200
Then just wait for the good news.

166
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:08,760
Madam. Don't keep secrets from me.
We're on the same side.

167
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:30,320
You're just helping me hand out flyers.
You didn't have to dress up.

168
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:34,240
If we dress normally,

169
00:15:34,320 --> 00:15:37,560
we'll look poor. We need to look rich.

170
00:15:37,640 --> 00:15:40,120
Rich enough that people
believe they can rely on us.

171
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:45,080
I'm not here to sell wealth.
I'm here to sell policies.

172
00:15:45,680 --> 00:15:48,480
Listen, Raiwin. Your father

173
00:15:48,560 --> 00:15:51,000
came up with good policies too.

174
00:15:51,080 --> 00:15:54,080
And what good does

175
00:15:54,160 --> 00:15:57,480
flaunting wealth do?
Does that really win people over?

176
00:15:57,560 --> 00:15:59,720
People want a good person
representing them.

177
00:15:59,800 --> 00:16:03,560
Listen, brand-new politician.

178
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:07,640
What do people get from having
a good person as their leader?

179
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:10,360
They get a good person
who develops the community.

180
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:14,120
And if the community develops,
what do the villagers personally get?

181
00:16:15,560 --> 00:16:17,800
But if they get a wealthy leader,

182
00:16:17,880 --> 00:16:21,000
then when they're in trouble,
they have someone rich to depend on.

183
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:23,360
That's how parasites are.

184
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:25,960
They want to attach
themselves to rich people.

185
00:16:26,040 --> 00:16:27,520
Thai-style democracy.

186
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:30,400
You look down on the locals too much.

187
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:37,600
When our country actually has equality,

188
00:16:37,680 --> 00:16:40,000
then you can come talk to me
about democracy.

189
00:16:40,880 --> 00:16:42,040
Come on.

190
00:16:43,760 --> 00:16:44,640
Put your jacket on.

191
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:58,800
Hello. Hello.

192
00:16:58,880 --> 00:17:00,480
Hello. I'm Raiwin.

193
00:17:00,560 --> 00:17:01,720
Please vote number one.

194
00:17:01,800 --> 00:17:03,120
Yes.

195
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:04,800
Aw.

196
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:06,880
So cute.

197
00:17:06,960 --> 00:17:08,920
Can I hold you?

198
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,000
-Thank you.
-Hello.

199
00:17:11,079 --> 00:17:12,520
Is this for me?

200
00:17:12,599 --> 00:17:14,440
Hello.

201
00:17:14,520 --> 00:17:15,920
Hold this for me.

202
00:17:16,640 --> 00:17:19,760
NUMBER 1
RAIWIN TRAIPONGRATCHATA

203
00:17:19,839 --> 00:17:20,720
Come on.

204
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:23,880
That way.

205
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:25,440
So cute.

206
00:17:28,359 --> 00:17:30,280
-Isn't he adorable?
-Very.

207
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:31,840
Take a picture for me.

208
00:17:32,360 --> 00:17:33,520
Sure.

209
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:37,320
-Ready?
-Look at the camera.

210
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:40,320
One, two, three.

211
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:43,240
Come get in the picture too. Come on.

212
00:17:44,360 --> 00:17:45,800
There!

213
00:17:45,880 --> 00:17:46,960
Look at the camera. Smile.

214
00:17:47,040 --> 00:17:49,440
One, two, three.

215
00:17:50,040 --> 00:17:50,960
Okay.

216
00:17:51,040 --> 00:17:53,760
Raiwin, if we ever have a child,

217
00:17:53,840 --> 00:17:55,480
our baby has to be this cute.

218
00:17:58,320 --> 00:18:01,000
-Okay.
-Hathaya is here too. Let's take pictures.

219
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:04,360
-Let's go take pictures with her.
-One, two, three.

220
00:18:04,440 --> 00:18:05,800
Beautiful.

221
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:09,480
Wait.

222
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,120
Excuse us.

223
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:17,040
Please support candidate
number one, Mr. Raiwin.

224
00:18:17,120 --> 00:18:18,440
Please support him.

225
00:18:18,520 --> 00:18:20,640
-Please vote for him.
-Thank you very much.

226
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:22,640
-Hello.
-Hello.

227
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:24,360
-Hello.
-Hello.

228
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:26,080
One, two, three.

229
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:29,240
-Very nice.
-Thank you.

230
00:18:29,320 --> 00:18:31,560
Please support us.
Vote for Raiwin, number one.

231
00:18:31,640 --> 00:18:32,760
Thank you very much.

232
00:18:35,760 --> 00:18:36,600
What's this?

233
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:37,760
He gave it to me.

234
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:39,560
Why are you here?

235
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:41,920
I brought Hathaya here.

236
00:18:43,280 --> 00:18:46,920
I told you not to have Hathaya
campaign for you.

237
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,360
I brought her myself.

238
00:18:48,440 --> 00:18:49,720
What's this to do with you?

239
00:18:49,800 --> 00:18:50,840
Oh?

240
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:54,680
Is there a rule against a younger brother
helping his older brother campaign?

241
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:56,880
Come on, Chayanee.

242
00:18:57,640 --> 00:18:59,680
Don't let jealousy ruin the campaign.

243
00:19:00,480 --> 00:19:01,320
Look around.

244
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:02,880
Everyone is watching.

245
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:06,400
Why don't we put on

246
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:08,640
a united family front?

247
00:19:08,720 --> 00:19:09,560
It'll help Raiwin.

248
00:19:09,640 --> 00:19:12,080
Come on over. Please, come over here.

249
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:14,560
Come on. Right here.

250
00:19:14,640 --> 00:19:16,360
Please come. Here.

251
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:19,000
We'll take some pictures with Hathaya too.

252
00:19:19,080 --> 00:19:20,960
What a lucky day.

253
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:23,240
Both of my sons are here together.

254
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:25,280
We're family. We're number one.

255
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:28,600
Let's all take a picture together.
Come here.

256
00:19:28,680 --> 00:19:30,720
Miss Chayanee, stand in the middle.

257
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:32,680
Son, stand right beside her.
Our future Chief.

258
00:19:32,760 --> 00:19:35,000
Everyone, come take pictures with us.

259
00:19:35,600 --> 00:19:37,280
Look at the camera.

260
00:19:37,360 --> 00:19:39,520
Smile. Everyone smile.

261
00:19:39,600 --> 00:19:42,480
We're team number one. Smile.

262
00:19:42,560 --> 00:19:43,680
Number one.

263
00:19:52,360 --> 00:19:55,040
Thanks for helping my son.

264
00:19:55,120 --> 00:19:58,640
Though I probably don't
even need to thank you.

265
00:19:58,720 --> 00:20:01,760
-Someone like you
-Number one!

266
00:20:01,840 --> 00:20:04,960
owes me plenty anyway.

267
00:20:06,080 --> 00:20:07,240
Wow, Uncle.

268
00:20:07,320 --> 00:20:10,000
You'd look a lot better
if you just kept quiet.

269
00:20:11,560 --> 00:20:12,520
Ramil.

270
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:15,040
Former Subdistrict Chief,
control yourself.

271
00:20:15,120 --> 00:20:18,040
We're in public. It won't look good.

272
00:20:18,640 --> 00:20:21,040
And you really don't have to thank me.

273
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:23,640
I'm doing this for Raiwin and Papang.

274
00:20:24,200 --> 00:20:26,480
I'm not doing a single thing for you.

275
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:29,000
Ramil.

276
00:20:32,600 --> 00:20:35,080
Uncle, I hate those two.

277
00:20:35,160 --> 00:20:37,120
Can you make them leave?

278
00:20:38,200 --> 00:20:40,480
Chayanee, calm down.

279
00:20:41,640 --> 00:20:44,120
If we throw them out now,
it won't be good for Raiwin.

280
00:20:46,320 --> 00:20:50,440
You need to be patient.

281
00:20:50,520 --> 00:20:52,400
That woman may be

282
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:55,360
the darling of the grassroots,

283
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:59,360
but you're

284
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:02,720
Raiwin's sweetheart.

285
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:06,600
And you're the real one.

286
00:21:10,360 --> 00:21:14,160
Vote number one. Please support us.

287
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:16,000
Vote number one.

288
00:21:16,080 --> 00:21:18,800
Yes. Please vote number one.

289
00:21:18,880 --> 00:21:21,280
-Please vote number one.
-Hello.

290
00:21:21,360 --> 00:21:24,080
Number one.

291
00:21:24,160 --> 00:21:25,440
Number one.

292
00:21:33,320 --> 00:21:36,080
No woman is interested
in a poor man, madam.

293
00:21:36,600 --> 00:21:38,080
They're all chasing appearances.

294
00:21:38,160 --> 00:21:39,520
So what do you want me to do?

295
00:21:39,600 --> 00:21:43,200
You need to get me clothes and accessories
that fit the part I'm playing.

296
00:21:46,360 --> 00:21:47,440
And what part is that?

297
00:21:48,040 --> 00:21:50,200
A wealthy tycoon
who owns a global travel agency.

298
00:21:57,440 --> 00:22:00,840
Minister? Yes, sir.

299
00:22:01,840 --> 00:22:04,280
Of course. Whatever you need.

300
00:22:04,360 --> 00:22:06,000
Where would you like to go this time?

301
00:22:06,080 --> 00:22:08,560
Would you like to follow the Olympic trail

302
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:12,560
in France or go skiing in Switzerland?

303
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:14,800
Of course. The snow is perfect right now.

304
00:22:15,840 --> 00:22:18,880
Absolutely. I'd be delighted.

305
00:22:19,720 --> 00:22:21,520
Yes, sir.

306
00:22:23,080 --> 00:22:26,360
Yes. No problem at all.

307
00:22:26,440 --> 00:22:28,880
A hundred thousand, a million,

308
00:22:29,480 --> 00:22:31,440
that's nothing. Anything for you, sir.

309
00:22:32,880 --> 00:22:35,160
Yes, sir.

310
00:22:36,280 --> 00:22:37,120
Sir--

311
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:10,960
Use this to buy clothes that fit the role.

312
00:23:13,400 --> 00:23:16,000
How about some money
for supporting actors too, madam?

313
00:23:16,880 --> 00:23:18,960
Why do you need anyone else?

314
00:23:19,040 --> 00:23:22,360
If you want to impress a woman,
you need to create a hero moment.

315
00:23:47,040 --> 00:23:48,000
Help. Help me.

316
00:23:48,080 --> 00:23:49,960
-My purse. My purse.
-I'll get it back.

317
00:23:50,040 --> 00:23:52,240
-Help.
-Stop. I said stop!

318
00:23:52,320 --> 00:23:54,640
Somebody help. A thief stole my purse.

319
00:23:54,720 --> 00:23:56,440
I told you to stop. Stop.

320
00:23:56,960 --> 00:23:59,000
Daeng. I told you to stop.

321
00:23:59,080 --> 00:24:01,960
Where the hell are you going?
I'm exhausted. Give it here.

322
00:24:02,040 --> 00:24:03,320
She's coming.

323
00:24:03,400 --> 00:24:04,560
Help.

324
00:24:04,640 --> 00:24:07,080
-Punch me.
-Somebody help.

325
00:24:07,160 --> 00:24:09,600
You didn't have to hit me
that hard. My turn.

326
00:24:09,680 --> 00:24:11,280
Hey!

327
00:24:11,360 --> 00:24:13,400
Don't run away.

328
00:24:13,480 --> 00:24:14,600
Be careful.

329
00:24:15,440 --> 00:24:17,320
Here's your purse.

330
00:24:17,400 --> 00:24:18,600
-Thank you.
-Wait here.

331
00:24:18,680 --> 00:24:20,480
I'm going after him.

332
00:24:20,560 --> 00:24:22,080
Be careful.

333
00:24:22,160 --> 00:24:23,720
-Stop!
-Help!

334
00:24:23,800 --> 00:24:26,240
-Somebody help. There's a thief.
-Stop!

335
00:24:33,040 --> 00:24:34,360
Is it too hot?

336
00:24:34,440 --> 00:24:36,120
-I'm good, totally fine.
-Can I have one?

337
00:24:36,200 --> 00:24:37,080
Yeah.

338
00:24:37,600 --> 00:24:39,000
-Hello.
-Hello.

339
00:24:39,080 --> 00:24:41,400
Please support candidate number one.

340
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:42,960
-Hello.
-Please support us.

341
00:24:43,040 --> 00:24:44,840
-Thank you.
-How much?

342
00:24:46,720 --> 00:24:48,960
The polling place
is just outside the village.

343
00:24:49,040 --> 00:24:51,240
It shouldn't cost much to get there.

344
00:24:51,320 --> 00:24:54,120
Going out to vote still costs money.

345
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:56,160
There should at least be pocket money.

346
00:24:56,240 --> 00:24:58,480
-Right?
-Right. We need some cash.

347
00:24:58,560 --> 00:25:01,240
Let's be frank. Other candidates pay 500.

348
00:25:01,320 --> 00:25:03,040
How much can you offer?

349
00:25:03,120 --> 00:25:05,800
Let's just see who pays the most.

350
00:25:05,880 --> 00:25:08,080
You know that's illegal.

351
00:25:08,160 --> 00:25:10,760
I'd rather you look at the policies.

352
00:25:11,280 --> 00:25:13,960
See which candidate
can actually improve your lives.

353
00:25:14,040 --> 00:25:17,120
Waste of time. The former
subdistrict chief said the same thing.

354
00:25:17,640 --> 00:25:19,680
Never delivered on any of it.
Empty promises.

355
00:25:19,760 --> 00:25:21,600
Exactly. We've heard it all before.

356
00:25:23,640 --> 00:25:25,800
But Raiwin isn't

357
00:25:25,880 --> 00:25:27,160
-a politician--
-Just go.

358
00:25:27,240 --> 00:25:29,160
Save it. You're wasting my time.

359
00:25:29,760 --> 00:25:30,840
Come on. Forget it.

360
00:25:31,360 --> 00:25:34,120
Let's go over there.
People are waiting for you.

361
00:25:34,760 --> 00:25:35,960
-Waste of time.
-Come.

362
00:25:36,920 --> 00:25:38,040
Everyone's the same.

363
00:25:49,560 --> 00:25:50,440
Hathaya.

364
00:25:55,720 --> 00:25:58,120
If you don't like the policies,
that's fine.

365
00:25:58,200 --> 00:26:01,440
Just give the flyers back.
Don't tear them up and litter.

366
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:04,640
Everyone is campaigning
to keep the community clean.

367
00:26:05,200 --> 00:26:08,080
Paper like this can clog the drains.

368
00:26:08,160 --> 00:26:11,200
Guys. She's angry just because
we said we won't vote for her guy.

369
00:26:11,280 --> 00:26:14,280
I'm not angry because you won't
vote for the candidate I support.

370
00:26:14,360 --> 00:26:16,000
It's because you're selling your voices.

371
00:26:16,080 --> 00:26:18,240
We're not selling them.

372
00:26:18,320 --> 00:26:21,040
We still have our voices.
And they're pretty loud, too.

373
00:26:21,120 --> 00:26:22,880
Come on, everyone. Let's hear your voices.

374
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:27,560
You complain that politicians are corrupt,

375
00:26:27,640 --> 00:26:30,320
but you're helping create
those corrupt politicians.

376
00:26:30,960 --> 00:26:33,520
You even bargain over
who pays more and who pays less.

377
00:26:33,600 --> 00:26:36,360
In the end, you're the ones
benefiting from it.

378
00:26:36,440 --> 00:26:39,400
We get 500 or 600 baht.
That barely pays for snacks and drinks.

379
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:43,320
But when politicians get into office,
they invent projects

380
00:26:43,400 --> 00:26:44,560
and pocket millions.

381
00:26:46,240 --> 00:26:47,880
I used to work as a contractor.

382
00:26:48,400 --> 00:26:51,320
Name one place in this country
where there aren't kickbacks.

383
00:26:51,400 --> 00:26:55,000
Once they're in office, they come up
with projects. Clock towers.

384
00:26:55,080 --> 00:26:58,400
Roads. Streetlights. They tear
things down, build them again,

385
00:26:58,480 --> 00:27:00,080
and take kickbacks every step of the way.

386
00:27:00,160 --> 00:27:04,400
You know corrupt politicians want to make
back what they spent getting elected.

387
00:27:05,880 --> 00:27:08,040
Then we can't allow parasitic politicians

388
00:27:08,120 --> 00:27:09,480
to take our tax money.

389
00:27:10,560 --> 00:27:12,880
And the reason
you complain about politicians

390
00:27:12,960 --> 00:27:15,080
is because you hate seeing them steal.

391
00:27:15,680 --> 00:27:17,560
If you don't want them stealing,

392
00:27:18,160 --> 00:27:21,640
then you can't sell your vote either.
You can't break the law.

393
00:27:21,720 --> 00:27:23,680
Everything has to start with us.

394
00:27:23,760 --> 00:27:26,280
How am I supposed to know
this candidate won't steal?

395
00:27:30,440 --> 00:27:31,680
Raiwin.

396
00:27:32,280 --> 00:27:35,440
Can you promise everyone here

397
00:27:35,520 --> 00:27:37,920
that you won't buy a single vote?

398
00:27:43,160 --> 00:27:44,840
There's no need for promises.

399
00:27:44,920 --> 00:27:46,720
My son, your future subdistrict chief,

400
00:27:47,440 --> 00:27:50,520
-is a generous and sincere man.
-I promise.

401
00:27:57,960 --> 00:28:00,440
I'll run an honest campaign.

402
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:04,000
And I promise that if I'm elected,

403
00:28:04,640 --> 00:28:06,800
I'll work as hard as I can.

404
00:28:07,480 --> 00:28:09,080
I will not engage in corruption.

405
00:28:11,160 --> 00:28:12,320
Please support number one.

406
00:28:12,400 --> 00:28:14,440
Number one.

407
00:28:14,520 --> 00:28:17,680
Number one.

408
00:28:17,760 --> 00:28:20,360
Number one.

409
00:28:21,960 --> 00:28:25,040
Number one.

410
00:28:25,120 --> 00:28:27,840
-Please vote number one.
-Thank you.

411
00:28:27,920 --> 00:28:29,040
Thank you.

412
00:28:30,600 --> 00:28:33,280
I'm out of flyers. Next time

413
00:28:33,360 --> 00:28:35,160
you should bring a lot more.

414
00:28:35,920 --> 00:28:40,240
That's great. Then more people
can read my policies and ideas.

415
00:28:40,320 --> 00:28:43,280
Thanks, Ramil. And thank you, Hathaya.

416
00:28:44,280 --> 00:28:46,000
I'm happy to help.

417
00:28:46,080 --> 00:28:48,480
But please keep the promise you made.

418
00:28:48,560 --> 00:28:50,200
If you break your word,

419
00:28:51,160 --> 00:28:53,240
the two of us will be on opposite sides.

420
00:28:55,040 --> 00:28:57,120
Are you threatening Raiwin?

421
00:28:57,920 --> 00:29:01,080
I'm not threatening him.
I mean it sincerely.

422
00:29:01,680 --> 00:29:05,320
I agreed to campaign for him
because I want to see clean politics.

423
00:29:18,680 --> 00:29:19,560
Hey.

424
00:29:20,080 --> 00:29:22,960
I think I'll stop by one more place
and hand out flyers.

425
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:26,480
No. I'm tired. I want to go home.

426
00:29:28,560 --> 00:29:31,840
Okay. Let's go eat.

427
00:29:53,040 --> 00:29:54,480
NUMBER 2
KRITSADA SIDEE

428
00:30:01,120 --> 00:30:02,600
I spoke with the police.

429
00:30:02,680 --> 00:30:05,040
They promised they'll catch the thief.

430
00:30:06,440 --> 00:30:08,720
It's really okay. I got my purse back,

431
00:30:08,800 --> 00:30:10,560
and all the money's there. That's enough.

432
00:30:11,160 --> 00:30:14,800
No. I still need to coordinate with
the police and make sure they catch him.

433
00:30:15,320 --> 00:30:18,080
If criminals go unpunished,
everyone is in danger.

434
00:30:18,160 --> 00:30:20,120
Thank you so much.

435
00:30:20,200 --> 00:30:22,280
You got hurt because of me.

436
00:30:22,360 --> 00:30:24,760
It was nothing. I was happy to help.

437
00:30:26,200 --> 00:30:29,200
I need to go.

438
00:30:29,280 --> 00:30:33,080
I have to take
the minister's family overseas.

439
00:30:34,240 --> 00:30:35,200
Excuse me.

440
00:30:35,280 --> 00:30:36,120
Alright.

441
00:30:44,120 --> 00:30:45,280
I'm really leaving now.

442
00:30:45,880 --> 00:30:48,360
-Thank you again.
-Of course.

443
00:30:51,080 --> 00:30:52,600
Stop me, damn it.

444
00:30:54,120 --> 00:30:58,080
Come on. One, two, three--

445
00:30:58,160 --> 00:30:59,360
Excuse me.

446
00:31:02,160 --> 00:31:03,080
Yes?

447
00:31:08,360 --> 00:31:09,440
Well,

448
00:31:10,240 --> 00:31:11,800
you helped me,

449
00:31:12,600 --> 00:31:14,440
and I still don't even know your name.

450
00:31:14,520 --> 00:31:16,280
You can call me Yai.

451
00:31:17,480 --> 00:31:19,040
All right, Yai.

452
00:31:21,800 --> 00:31:25,080
If I get the chance,

453
00:31:25,160 --> 00:31:28,120
I'd like to treat you to a meal
to thank you for helping me.

454
00:31:29,120 --> 00:31:32,120
Could we exchange contacts?

455
00:31:33,760 --> 00:31:35,600
I never help anyone expecting a reward.

456
00:31:36,400 --> 00:31:40,120
But I suppose there's no harm

457
00:31:41,200 --> 00:31:42,160
in getting acquainted.

458
00:31:46,760 --> 00:31:48,080
Can I scan your code?

459
00:31:48,840 --> 00:31:50,840
Sure. I'll scan yours.

460
00:31:53,200 --> 00:31:54,200
There. All done.

461
00:31:55,880 --> 00:31:56,960
Thank you again.

462
00:31:57,040 --> 00:31:58,440
My pleasure.

463
00:32:10,680 --> 00:32:13,920
It's strange. We've only just met,

464
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:16,720
but I feel like
I've known you for a long time.

465
00:32:20,840 --> 00:32:22,400
Really?

466
00:32:23,040 --> 00:32:25,200
I feel the same way.

467
00:32:32,200 --> 00:32:34,400
Mom.

468
00:32:35,040 --> 00:32:38,400
Your phone keeps buzzing.
Who are you texting?

469
00:32:38,480 --> 00:32:41,120
Yai. The man I told you about.

470
00:32:41,200 --> 00:32:42,640
The one who helped me.

471
00:32:43,840 --> 00:32:46,800
What does he look like? I want to see him.

472
00:32:46,880 --> 00:32:50,880
He doesn't have any pictures posted.
Rich people are like that.

473
00:32:50,960 --> 00:32:52,960
They like keeping a low profile.

474
00:32:53,480 --> 00:32:56,560
But he's handsome in person.

475
00:32:57,600 --> 00:33:00,800
Polite and very well-groomed too.

476
00:33:00,880 --> 00:33:02,880
Really, Mom?

477
00:33:02,960 --> 00:33:04,920
Are you falling for him?

478
00:33:05,760 --> 00:33:08,160
Hey. What are you talking about?

479
00:33:08,240 --> 00:33:10,800
We just met.

480
00:33:10,880 --> 00:33:12,600
I don't feel anything.

481
00:33:14,080 --> 00:33:16,320
You can't judge
someone's heart by their face.

482
00:33:16,400 --> 00:33:18,560
Be careful who you talk to.

483
00:33:20,160 --> 00:33:21,280
I know.

484
00:33:21,360 --> 00:33:24,080
Go take a shower.
I'll dry your hair afterward.

485
00:33:24,160 --> 00:33:25,560
-Okay.
-Go.

486
00:33:25,640 --> 00:33:26,480
Okay.

487
00:33:35,120 --> 00:33:38,360
Talk to you later.
I'm about to board my flight.

488
00:33:38,440 --> 00:33:40,240
Have a safe trip.

489
00:33:41,160 --> 00:33:44,720
I'll send you some beautiful pictures

490
00:33:44,800 --> 00:33:47,200
from Switzerland.

491
00:33:53,680 --> 00:33:55,240
Sending her a message is enough.

492
00:33:55,320 --> 00:33:57,960
Do you really need
all those sweet little stickers too?

493
00:33:58,040 --> 00:33:59,640
Are you jealous, madam?

494
00:34:00,680 --> 00:34:03,960
Are you crazy? You and I
are nothing to each other.

495
00:34:04,040 --> 00:34:05,360
Why would I be jealous?

496
00:34:05,440 --> 00:34:07,280
I'm joking.

497
00:34:07,800 --> 00:34:10,880
Don't worry. You can relax.

498
00:34:10,960 --> 00:34:13,199
The fish has taken the bait.

499
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:17,040
Good. Make Hathai trust you,

500
00:34:17,120 --> 00:34:19,080
then lure her in according to the plan.

501
00:34:19,159 --> 00:34:23,320
You don't need to worry about that.
My friends run several gambling dens.

502
00:34:23,400 --> 00:34:25,760
I'll personally take her there.

503
00:34:27,719 --> 00:34:29,960
Make sure she gets buried
in gambling debt.

504
00:34:30,480 --> 00:34:32,159
I'll handle the rest.

505
00:34:34,600 --> 00:34:36,440
-Wait.
-What?

506
00:34:36,520 --> 00:34:37,560
You're leaving already?

507
00:34:37,639 --> 00:34:40,159
Of course. What if someone sees me?

508
00:34:40,239 --> 00:34:44,080
And don't show your face around
the staff quarters or the main house.

509
00:34:44,679 --> 00:34:48,000
Don't let anyone realize you work for me.

510
00:34:49,400 --> 00:34:50,800
Understood.

511
00:35:03,720 --> 00:35:05,040
Widows

512
00:35:06,440 --> 00:35:08,040
can never resist me.

513
00:35:20,040 --> 00:35:21,600
-Please vote number one.
-Number one.

514
00:35:21,680 --> 00:35:24,600
-Thank you. Hello.
-Get out!

515
00:35:24,680 --> 00:35:27,120
Get out. Get out of here.

516
00:35:27,200 --> 00:35:29,480
-Get out.
-Calm down.

517
00:35:29,560 --> 00:35:32,040
-Get out! Get out of here.
-What?

518
00:35:32,120 --> 00:35:34,320
Calm down. What happened?

519
00:35:34,400 --> 00:35:36,240
You parasitic politicians.

520
00:35:36,320 --> 00:35:38,080
That's enough.

521
00:35:38,160 --> 00:35:40,800
I'm calling the police
and having you all arrested for assault.

522
00:35:40,880 --> 00:35:43,880
Call them. Go ahead.
I'll report you for buying votes.

523
00:35:44,960 --> 00:35:46,200
What are you talking about?

524
00:35:46,280 --> 00:35:49,440
You promised to run an honest campaign,

525
00:35:49,520 --> 00:35:51,040
but you're buying votes behind us.

526
00:35:51,720 --> 00:35:55,000
Raiwin, did you do what he says?

527
00:35:57,120 --> 00:36:00,880
No. I promised I wouldn't buy votes.

528
00:36:01,880 --> 00:36:04,160
Do you have any evidence
that we bought votes?

529
00:36:04,240 --> 00:36:06,640
Evidence?

530
00:36:06,720 --> 00:36:08,560
Lak is the evidence.
He took money from you.

531
00:36:08,640 --> 00:36:09,640
Lak.

532
00:36:10,400 --> 00:36:12,000
Tell them. Who gave you that money?

533
00:36:14,720 --> 00:36:16,240
Please support number one.

534
00:36:18,960 --> 00:36:20,160
Number one.

535
00:36:25,680 --> 00:36:27,400
NUMBER 2
KRITSADA SIDEE

536
00:36:29,880 --> 00:36:31,840
Well…

537
00:36:31,920 --> 00:36:33,520
You corrupt politicians.

538
00:36:33,600 --> 00:36:36,360
Nothing but fake appearances.
Pretending to be good people.

539
00:36:36,440 --> 00:36:37,960
Get out.

540
00:36:38,040 --> 00:36:40,040
-Get out.
-Calm down.

541
00:36:40,120 --> 00:36:42,800
-I'm reporting you for vote buying.
-Raiwin.

542
00:36:42,880 --> 00:36:45,560
Where is Mr. Saksit?

543
00:36:50,680 --> 00:36:54,280
You look beautiful today, Ms. Hathai.
Where are you going?

544
00:36:54,360 --> 00:36:55,760
I have something to take care of.

545
00:36:56,800 --> 00:36:58,720
Would you like me to go with you?

546
00:36:58,800 --> 00:37:02,160
No. Stay here and help out.
Father may need something.

547
00:37:07,880 --> 00:37:09,200
-I'm going now.
-All right.

548
00:37:15,800 --> 00:37:17,720
How did Pong fool her?

549
00:37:17,800 --> 00:37:19,720
How did Hathai fall for it so easily?

550
00:37:21,840 --> 00:37:24,240
Older widows are all the same.

551
00:37:24,320 --> 00:37:27,480
Once they see a handsome man
who looks wealthy and successful,

552
00:37:27,560 --> 00:37:29,880
they all melt.

553
00:37:31,960 --> 00:37:33,560
You too, madam?

554
00:37:33,640 --> 00:37:37,240
Are you crazy? I don't go for workers.

555
00:37:37,320 --> 00:37:40,480
Madam, workers are still men.

556
00:37:40,560 --> 00:37:43,040
And some of them have bodies
that are very nice to look at.

557
00:37:43,120 --> 00:37:45,080
My mouth is watering.

558
00:37:46,360 --> 00:37:50,200
Pong is slippery, though.
You need to be careful around him.

559
00:37:50,280 --> 00:37:51,840
I know.

560
00:37:52,360 --> 00:37:54,480
You always expect the worst from everyone.

561
00:37:54,560 --> 00:37:57,240
That attitude is why nobody wants you.

562
00:38:01,880 --> 00:38:03,800
I was only trying to help.

563
00:38:05,400 --> 00:38:08,080
Honestly, Chamoi,
what did I do in a past life

564
00:38:08,160 --> 00:38:10,040
to deserve people like this?

565
00:38:11,040 --> 00:38:12,160
Please support us.

566
00:38:12,240 --> 00:38:15,040
Sorry. Wrong flyer.

567
00:38:16,880 --> 00:38:19,400
Ramil. What the hell are you doing?

568
00:38:19,480 --> 00:38:23,160
I didn't want to get involved, but what
you're doing is illegal. Put it away.

569
00:38:24,080 --> 00:38:25,160
Mr. Saksit,

570
00:38:25,240 --> 00:38:28,960
do you even realize what you're doing?
You're hurting your own son.

571
00:38:29,040 --> 00:38:31,680
Me? Hurting him? I'm helping him.

572
00:38:32,400 --> 00:38:36,120
You two are unbelievably naive.
Do you know that the two of you

573
00:38:36,200 --> 00:38:39,320
are going to cost Raiwin the election?

574
00:38:39,400 --> 00:38:41,920
You still don't understand
that what you're doing is wrong.

575
00:38:42,520 --> 00:38:45,640
Wrong? Buying votes is wrong?

576
00:38:46,520 --> 00:38:49,520
Look over there. Do you see that?
They're everywhere.

577
00:38:50,600 --> 00:38:53,040
That's what being a good person gets you.

578
00:38:54,800 --> 00:38:58,520
I buy votes because I'm playing the game.

579
00:38:58,600 --> 00:39:01,760
This isn't some morality contest.

580
00:39:01,840 --> 00:39:04,200
This is a contest measured in money.

581
00:39:04,280 --> 00:39:06,400
Record this. They're buying votes.

582
00:39:08,280 --> 00:39:09,840
-Get it on video.
-Got it.

583
00:39:10,560 --> 00:39:11,480
Dad.

584
00:39:12,600 --> 00:39:14,840
They're going to go after me.
What are you going to do?

585
00:39:16,880 --> 00:39:19,280
You have to fix this.
Raiwin has to become the Chief.

586
00:39:22,040 --> 00:39:25,560
This is nothing. I'll take care of it.

587
00:39:25,640 --> 00:39:26,800
Oh.

588
00:39:26,880 --> 00:39:29,440
Hello, everyone.

589
00:39:29,520 --> 00:39:30,920
Hello.

590
00:39:31,560 --> 00:39:33,680
Have you all not received your things yet?

591
00:39:34,360 --> 00:39:37,720
I had a delivery rider
bring something for everyone.

592
00:39:37,800 --> 00:39:38,640
Did you get it?

593
00:39:39,240 --> 00:39:42,080
Did you? So you haven't gotten it yet?

594
00:39:42,960 --> 00:39:44,960
Here it comes.

595
00:39:45,040 --> 00:39:46,160
Here it is.

596
00:39:46,240 --> 00:39:47,960
Your food order is here. Open it.

597
00:39:48,040 --> 00:39:49,840
Open it. Take a look.

598
00:39:49,920 --> 00:39:50,640
NUMBER 1
RAIWIN TRAIPONGRATCHATA

599
00:39:50,720 --> 00:39:52,080
Well? Do you like it?

600
00:39:52,160 --> 00:39:55,440
Now that you've got your food, enjoy it.

601
00:39:56,040 --> 00:39:57,880
Go ahead. Take it.

602
00:39:59,680 --> 00:40:01,040
Come on, everyone.

603
00:40:01,120 --> 00:40:02,800
-Let's go eat something good.
-Thank you.

604
00:40:02,880 --> 00:40:05,280
-Hey, wait. My delivery bag.
-Come on.

605
00:40:13,000 --> 00:40:14,320
Well?

606
00:40:14,840 --> 00:40:16,880
I solved the whole problem for you.

607
00:40:18,040 --> 00:40:19,160
Learn from this.

608
00:40:20,040 --> 00:40:23,440
Money is God. Money can buy anything.

609
00:40:24,040 --> 00:40:26,160
But I didn't want to use this method, Dad.

610
00:40:26,240 --> 00:40:29,040
Then what method are you going to use?

611
00:40:29,120 --> 00:40:31,440
This is what the villagers want.

612
00:40:31,520 --> 00:40:33,640
The election is only a few days away.

613
00:40:33,720 --> 00:40:37,680
You could walk until your shoes fall apart
and nobody would vote for you.

614
00:40:38,280 --> 00:40:40,320
At least give me a chance to prove myself.

615
00:40:44,600 --> 00:40:48,720
But there really isn't much time left.

616
00:40:49,240 --> 00:40:51,120
Do whatever it takes
to get into office first.

617
00:40:51,200 --> 00:40:53,480
Then prove yourself
through your work afterward.

618
00:40:55,440 --> 00:40:58,160
I'll do whatever it takes to make sure
Raiwin becomes the Chief.

619
00:40:59,800 --> 00:41:01,600
If you button the first button wrong,

620
00:41:02,120 --> 00:41:04,240
the whole shirt will end up crooked.

621
00:41:05,680 --> 00:41:07,440
Money can buy many things,

622
00:41:08,000 --> 00:41:10,760
but that dirty money can't buy me.

623
00:41:11,720 --> 00:41:13,080
What are you planning to do?

624
00:41:13,680 --> 00:41:15,040
I already told you.

625
00:41:15,560 --> 00:41:18,600
If you buy votes or break the law,

626
00:41:18,680 --> 00:41:20,160
I'll stand against you.

627
00:41:20,920 --> 00:41:22,640
Then call. Go ahead.

628
00:41:22,720 --> 00:41:24,680
Call the police and have me arrested.

629
00:41:25,680 --> 00:41:27,280
Don't challenge me.

630
00:41:27,880 --> 00:41:30,760
Really? Ramil.

631
00:41:31,600 --> 00:41:34,200
Weren't you the one who said
you were going to help Raiwin?

632
00:41:34,840 --> 00:41:36,960
And Papang?

633
00:41:37,560 --> 00:41:39,560
But if you report this,

634
00:41:39,640 --> 00:41:41,560
Raiwin could end up going to prison.

635
00:41:42,520 --> 00:41:44,960
I don't know. Go ahead.

636
00:41:45,040 --> 00:41:47,360
Call the police. Have them arrest us.

637
00:41:50,040 --> 00:41:51,720
But you're the one breaking the law.

638
00:41:51,800 --> 00:41:53,080
Not Raiwin.

639
00:41:54,480 --> 00:41:55,320
Oh, really?

640
00:41:55,400 --> 00:41:57,880
If news about me gets out,

641
00:41:57,960 --> 00:41:59,920
think carefully. Do you honestly believe

642
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:02,360
anyone will still vote for Raiwin?

643
00:42:03,000 --> 00:42:05,760
It directly affects him.

644
00:42:09,040 --> 00:42:11,200
And if you really intend
to put me in prison,

645
00:42:11,280 --> 00:42:13,200
do you have any witnesses?

646
00:42:14,080 --> 00:42:16,160
Go into the community right now.

647
00:42:16,240 --> 00:42:19,280
I guarantee not a single villager
will testify for you.

648
00:42:19,840 --> 00:42:23,920
They've all taken my money.

649
00:42:24,000 --> 00:42:26,000
You broke the law

650
00:42:26,080 --> 00:42:28,520
and you're still proud of the result?

651
00:42:30,520 --> 00:42:32,200
You two really live in a fantasy world.

652
00:42:32,720 --> 00:42:34,760
I live in the real world.

653
00:42:35,680 --> 00:42:37,320
Get out. Go back

654
00:42:37,400 --> 00:42:41,360
to your imaginary perfect world. Go.

655
00:42:48,520 --> 00:42:52,480
Here are your flyers. I don't think
they'll be of any use to me anymore.

656
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:07,400
We still have much to do.

657
00:43:08,240 --> 00:43:09,680
Come on.

658
00:43:32,040 --> 00:43:34,560
Have we completely
lost hope in politicians?

659
00:43:35,320 --> 00:43:36,240
No.

660
00:43:39,040 --> 00:43:42,440
I still believe there are
good people in this country.

661
00:43:43,640 --> 00:43:45,320
Good politicians too.

662
00:43:49,640 --> 00:43:53,520
Don't be upset. You did your best.

663
00:43:56,040 --> 00:43:57,720
And I'm not giving up either.

664
00:43:59,240 --> 00:44:00,560
What are you going to do?

665
00:44:03,680 --> 00:44:06,120
No matter who becomes subdistrict chief,

666
00:44:07,280 --> 00:44:09,040
I'm going to scrutinize
everything they do.

667
00:44:10,360 --> 00:44:13,760
I won't let corrupt people
steal my tax money.

668
00:44:16,840 --> 00:44:18,360
What if that person

669
00:44:19,320 --> 00:44:21,520
is Raiwin? Your own brother?

670
00:44:23,440 --> 00:44:25,080
If he's really corrupt,

671
00:44:28,320 --> 00:44:29,720
I won't let him get away with it.

672
00:44:40,480 --> 00:44:42,480
Yai, thank you so much

673
00:44:42,560 --> 00:44:44,520
for having lunch with me today.

674
00:44:46,080 --> 00:44:47,360
It's my pleasure.

675
00:44:47,440 --> 00:44:50,320
I came straight here to see you
as soon as I got off the plane.

676
00:44:52,360 --> 00:44:56,040
Actually, I wanted to bring you
a designer handbag,

677
00:44:56,120 --> 00:44:58,640
but I had to look after
the minister's family,

678
00:44:58,720 --> 00:45:00,800
so I didn't have any personal time.

679
00:45:00,880 --> 00:45:01,960
Here.

680
00:45:03,280 --> 00:45:07,200
I brought you
a few small things. Some clothes

681
00:45:07,280 --> 00:45:08,800
and chocolates. I hope you like them.

682
00:45:09,720 --> 00:45:11,440
Thank you so much.

683
00:45:11,520 --> 00:45:13,720
Next time, I won't forget.

684
00:45:13,800 --> 00:45:16,160
I promise I'll bring you
a designer handbag.

685
00:45:16,760 --> 00:45:18,120
That's really not necessary.

686
00:45:18,200 --> 00:45:21,600
Just thinking of me
and bringing something is enough.

687
00:45:24,800 --> 00:45:25,880
Hathai.

688
00:45:26,440 --> 00:45:29,840
Do you have anywhere to go after this?

689
00:45:32,320 --> 00:45:35,920
No. I don't have anything else planned.

690
00:45:36,000 --> 00:45:39,440
Whenever I come back from a trip,
I like to relax

691
00:45:39,520 --> 00:45:42,600
and hang out with friends.

692
00:45:42,680 --> 00:45:44,800
Would you like to come with me?

693
00:45:47,920 --> 00:45:51,080
Where are you going, Yai?

694
00:46:09,640 --> 00:46:10,520
Come in.

695
00:46:20,160 --> 00:46:22,000
I like to relax here.

696
00:46:28,760 --> 00:46:31,400
Everyone in here is a friend of mine.

697
00:46:33,000 --> 00:46:36,200
When we get time, we come here to drink
and gamble a little to relieve stress.

698
00:46:36,280 --> 00:46:38,040
Please come in, Hathai.

699
00:46:40,200 --> 00:46:42,840
I'm sorry.

700
00:46:42,920 --> 00:46:44,240
Are you disgusted by me?

701
00:46:45,440 --> 00:46:48,520
No, I'm not. It's just…

702
00:46:50,720 --> 00:46:54,360
I promised my daughter

703
00:46:54,440 --> 00:46:56,160
I wouldn't gamble anymore.

704
00:46:56,920 --> 00:46:59,480
Your daughter sounds wonderful.

705
00:46:59,560 --> 00:47:01,080
She really cares about her mother.

706
00:47:02,080 --> 00:47:03,560
How about this?

707
00:47:04,160 --> 00:47:05,880
I promise

708
00:47:05,960 --> 00:47:10,000
I'll keep it secret.
I won't tell your daughter.

709
00:47:18,160 --> 00:47:19,120
Come on.

710
00:47:22,200 --> 00:47:25,080
I'm really sorry.

711
00:47:25,160 --> 00:47:27,040
I don't want to disappoint my daughter.

712
00:47:29,480 --> 00:47:31,480
And you're not afraid of disappointing me?

713
00:47:37,960 --> 00:47:39,000
Hathai.

714
00:47:39,520 --> 00:47:42,160
I've never brought another woman here.

715
00:47:42,920 --> 00:47:45,120
I consider this place private.

716
00:47:48,680 --> 00:47:50,880
I only bring someone here
if she's special to me.

717
00:47:53,880 --> 00:47:54,880
Come inside.

718
00:47:59,880 --> 00:48:00,800
Please.

719
00:48:02,280 --> 00:48:03,720
I'm really sorry.

720
00:48:10,960 --> 00:48:12,120
Pong.

721
00:48:13,320 --> 00:48:16,680
You got her all the way to the den.
Why did you let her leave?

722
00:48:16,760 --> 00:48:20,320
I want her drowning in debt. Then she'll
start stealing and selling off her stuff.

723
00:48:20,400 --> 00:48:23,520
After that, Father will throw her out.
Do you understand?

724
00:48:23,600 --> 00:48:27,200
I did everything I could, madam. I tried
convincing her. I flirted with her.

725
00:48:27,280 --> 00:48:29,840
Nothing worked. Try to understand.

726
00:48:31,240 --> 00:48:33,000
If you can't do it,
then stop making excuses.

727
00:48:33,080 --> 00:48:34,760
You really are useless.

728
00:48:34,840 --> 00:48:36,200
I'll have to find someone else.

729
00:48:36,280 --> 00:48:39,080
-Hey. Wait, madam.
-What now?

730
00:48:39,160 --> 00:48:42,280
Give me another chance. Do you know

731
00:48:43,080 --> 00:48:45,080
I even went to a spa.

732
00:48:45,160 --> 00:48:47,400
I had my entire body scrubbed.

733
00:48:47,920 --> 00:48:49,680
My skin is smooth, and I smell great.

734
00:48:50,400 --> 00:48:53,560
If you don't believe me,

735
00:48:54,280 --> 00:48:55,840
you can feel for yourself.

736
00:48:55,920 --> 00:48:58,120
Actually, I'd like you

737
00:48:59,240 --> 00:49:00,360
to feel my whole body.

738
00:49:02,200 --> 00:49:03,520
Start here…

739
00:49:06,280 --> 00:49:09,320
Hm? Why did you stop?

740
00:49:25,000 --> 00:49:26,800
You messed up this time.

741
00:49:26,880 --> 00:49:30,040
Next time, don't let your catch get away.

742
00:49:30,120 --> 00:49:31,400
NEXT EPISODE

743
00:49:31,480 --> 00:49:34,640
Do you know why
I still have feelings for you?

744
00:49:34,720 --> 00:49:37,040
Because you care
about other people's feelings.

745
00:49:37,120 --> 00:49:39,200
You're with Chayanee.

746
00:49:44,120 --> 00:49:45,560
Chayanee, stop!

747
00:49:45,640 --> 00:49:47,560
Stop thinking only about yourself.

748
00:49:47,640 --> 00:49:49,640
Think about me for once.

749
00:49:49,720 --> 00:49:50,760
Then,

750
00:49:51,280 --> 00:49:54,680
I'll put a cold compress on it for you.

751
00:51:46,440 --> 00:51:51,480
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
